  "changelog": "Initial release of roundtable-forge \u2014 a router skill for managing structured, multi-agent, cross-disciplinary roundtable discussions.\n\n- Routes user questions into roundtable discussions featuring real, historical, or fictional characters as independent agents.\n- Supports various discussion structures (standard, six hats, delphi, world cafe, fishbone) and output formats (minutes, podcast, argument graph).\n- Includes dynamic agent selection and coordination via a Conductor, with real-time shared Memory and a persistent argument graph.\n- Integrates with subagent runtime tools when supported for true multi-agent execution.\n- Designed for natural, in-depth exploration with traceable argumentation and flexible workflows.",
